  "findings": [
    {
      "level": "warn",
      "id": "version-drift",
      "lines": [
        "Version drift: appinfo/info.xml says 2.43.0, package.json says 1.0.0.",
        "  The App Store and the server read info.xml; everything on the node side reads package.json. Whichever is behind, a release ends up carrying two version numbers, and only one of them reaches the user."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "warn",
      "id": "repository-link",
      "lines": [
        "appinfo/info.xml states no <repository>.",
        "  <repository> is the only machine-readable link from a published release back to the source it was built from, and <bugs> is where the App Store page sends a report. Without them a user of the release has no way back to the project."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "warn",
      "id": "script-without-config",
      "lines": [
        "composer.json script psalm calls psalm, and no Psalm configuration is in the checkout.",
        "  psalm --threads=1 --no-cache",
        "  The command is there to be run, so whoever runs it gets a tool that has nothing to go by - and CI, if it runs the script, reports the failure as the change under test."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "app-id",
      "lines": [
        "The app id is educai, the checkout directory is talk-ai.",
        "  The server finds an app by its directory name, so the installed directory has to be named after the id. A checkout can be named anything, which is why this is a note and not a defect - but a tarball built from this directory name would not load."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "nextcloud-support",
      "lines": [
        "Declares Nextcloud 30 to 35; the oldest maintained major is 32 (as of 2026-09), the newest released 35 (the release tags of nextcloud/server).",
        "  min-version 30 reaches below the oldest maintained major (32), which means the code has to keep working with APIs that are no longer tested upstream."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "php-support",
      "lines": [
        "PHP floor stated once: composer.json requires php ^8.1; appinfo/info.xml declares no php dependency.",
        "  Nothing contradicts anything here. Stating it in both places is what keeps a composer install from resolving packages for a PHP the server will not run."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "node-version",
      "lines": [
        "Node 22 stated in .nvmrc, within package.json engines.node ^22.0.0.",
        "  Not stated in node-version in the workflows, so nothing keeps the other places from drifting away from it."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "tooling",
      "lines": [
        "Tooling in the checkout: ESLint (.eslintrc.cjs, superseded form), Stylelint (stylelint.config.cjs), PHPUnit (tests/phpunit.xml), PHP-CS-Fixer (.php-cs-fixer.dist.php).",
        " ESLint is configured in .eslintrc.cjs: ESLint 9 reads the flat config only; the eslintrc form, an .eslintrc file or the eslintConfig key in package.json, is ignored unless the run is pinned to ESLint 8.",
        " No Psalm configuration: the PHP side has no static analysis, which is what catches a wrong type before the server does.",
        " No REUSE configuration: licensing is not machine-checkable, which the App Store and every distribution ask for.",
        " No EditorConfig configuration: indentation is whatever each contributor's editor does."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "license-drift",
      "lines": [
        "Licence agpl (appinfo/info.xml), AGPL-3.0-or-later (package.json, composer.json).",
        "  agpl in appinfo/info.xml is a deprecated App Store value, shown there as AGPLv3+, which is AGPL-3.0-or-later. An SPDX id there needs a <nextcloud> min-version of 31 or higher.",
        "  No LICENSES/ directory, so the licence text itself is not in the checkout, which is what REUSE and the distributions check for."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "ok",
      "id": "lockfiles",
      "lines": [
        "package-lock.json (lockfileVersion 3) and composer.lock in the checkout."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "ok",
      "id": "ncmake-bootstrap",
      "lines": [
        "The ncmake bootstrap stub is in place (21 lines)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "ok",
      "id": "runtime-dirs-not-shipped",
      "lines": [
        "Every directory the shipped PHP reaches through __DIR__ and the frontend through linkTo is in the shipped file set (the ncmake core and ncmake.mk)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "ok",
      "id": "unreferenced-dependencies",
      "lines": [
        "All 16 declared packages are named somewhere in the checkout, 1 of them by convention."
      ]
    }
  ]
